Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:44:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] [tier 0] deepseek-v4.1: tool namespaces in the chat encoding

DeepSeek added tool namespaces to the checkpoint's reference
encoding/encoding.py (dba1be0a40aa) after SGLang's port was written:
a tool may carry a namespace; the prompt shows namespace::name and a
parsed call returns the bare name plus a namespace field on the tool
call (absent when there is none). The reference's other later change,
current-turn thinking and tool-result image order (314113f8a7da), is
already in SGLang as #44751.

tools/dsv41-encoding-check.py in the public repo compares the prompts
and parses with the reference byte for byte.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C2UBZdnrDZSBh8yQz8rc9g
